"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Review\n\nAs a light drizzle began to fall, we took refuge in a place where we could relax and enjoy a cup of coffee.  \nIt often pops up when searching for cafes in Geoje because it's so famous, so I was worried there wouldn't be any seats, but perhaps due to the bad weather, we were lucky enough to find a spot.  \n\nInside the cafe was a resident cat named Donggo.  \nBecause of the cat's aloof demeanor, I wanted to pet him but didn't dare to make a move, quickly ordering coffee and an egg tart instead.  \n\nThe coffee had a rich, nutty flavor just the way we like it, and the egg tart we ordered alongside it had an intriguingly scorched surface that gave off a subtle caramel aroma, which was delightful.  \n\nWhile we were relaxing with our coffee, more and more guests began trickling in before we knew it.  \nDonggo had nestled comfortably into the arms of another guest nearby, resting peacefully, and I felt so envious of the guest bonding with him.  \n\nI secretly hoped he might come over to our side, but seeing him sound asleep in that guest's lap without moving at all filled me with both jealousy and regret.  \nIf we visit again next time, I'll definitely have to sit near Donggo and gently coax him to come over.  \n\nIt was a truly lovely cafe where we could spend some leisurely time on a rainy day.\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"